package from the Ubuntu repositories, as well as the GNOME NetHack GUI
package. It's all pretty solid, except for one glaring, really
incredibly irritating bug.
If I don't exit NetHack with the save command (i.e. I just use the
"quit" command or close the window of the GUI), the next time I start
NetHack (in either console or GUI mode) I get the message "There is
already a game in progress under your name. Destroy old game?" and I am
given the options of yes or no. If I choose no, the game simply exits.
Choosing "yes" is the only way to continue playing, and then I have to
start over.
As you can probably imagine, this makes me so happy I could just shit.
I usually use the GUI, and I often forget to exit with Ctrl-S rather
than just clicking the X. As I mentioned before, however, I get this
problem with the terminal-based version as well. Has anyone else had
